# Neo Analyzer parameters (docs/specs/machines.md §5). The order is permanent: songs and presets
# store values by position. Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoAnalyzer
namespace NeoBuzz.Analyzer
class NeoAnalyzerMachine
summary Analyzer that passes audio through untouched and shows its spectrum (FFT with peak hold, third-octave bars), loudness (momentary, short-term and integrated LUFS, loudness range, true peak) and stereo image (correlation, width, goniometer). Insert it anywhere to watch a signal; machine_readings returns its numbers, which are the analysis library's (analyze measures the same way).

group Spectrum
Smoothing   "Smoothing"   0 3    2    enum 1/24_oct 1/12_oct 1/6_oct 1/3_oct   | Width of the band each point of the spectrum curve sums: narrow resolves single tones; 1/3 oct draws through the third-octave bars
Speed       "Speed"       0 3    1    enum Fast Medium Slow Very_slow          | How fast the spectrum follows the signal: averaging over about 0.1, 0.3, 1 or 3 s
Hold        "Peak hold"   0 1000 475  time 0.25 20                             | How long peaks hold before they fall: the spectrum's peak curve and bars, and the true-peak marker
Tilt        "Tilt"        0 2    0    enum 0_dB/oct 3_dB/oct 4.5_dB/oct        | Display slope around 1 kHz (the readings never tilt): 0 shows pink noise flat, 3 shows a typical finished mix about flat, 4.5 leans brighter
group Loudness
Target      "Target"      0 360  220  db -36 0                                 | The loudness (LUFS, written in dB) the meters are coloured against: −14 for streaming, −23 for broadcast
Reset       "Reset"       0 1    0    switch                                   | On: the integrated loudness, loudness range, maxima and held peaks start again. Turn it Off, then On, for the next reset

# What the analyzer measures (NeoAnalyzerMachine.Readings, machine_readings). Windows end now.
reading momentary_lufs        LUFS  | Loudness of the last 400 ms (BS.1770 momentary)
reading short_term_lufs       LUFS  | Loudness of the last 3 s (short-term)
reading integrated_lufs       LUFS  | Gated integrated loudness since the reset (BS.1770)
reading range_lu              LU    | Loudness range since the reset (EBU Tech 3342)
reading true_peak_dbtp        dBTP  | The highest true peak since the reset (4× oversampled, BS.1770 Annex 2)
reading momentary_max_lufs    LUFS  | The loudest 400 ms since the reset
reading short_term_max_lufs   LUFS  | The loudest 3 s since the reset
reading seconds               s     | Time measured since the reset
reading correlation           ratio | Correlation of left and right over the last 3 s: 1 mono, 0 unrelated, −1 opposed
reading width                 ratio | Side over mid energy over the last 3 s: 0 mono, 1 unrelated channels, above 1 when they oppose
reading sub_db                dB    | Level of 20–60 Hz over the last 3 s, dB RMS (a full-scale sine reads −3 dB)
reading low_db                dB    | Level of 60–250 Hz over the last 3 s, dB RMS
reading low_mid_db            dB    | Level of 250–500 Hz over the last 3 s, dB RMS
reading mid_db                dB    | Level of 500 Hz – 2 kHz over the last 3 s, dB RMS
reading high_mid_db           dB    | Level of 2–4 kHz over the last 3 s, dB RMS
reading presence_db           dB    | Level of 4–6 kHz over the last 3 s, dB RMS
reading air_db                dB    | Level of 6–20 kHz over the last 3 s, dB RMS
